From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:34:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] acp_thread: read the Claude task _meta on v2 session info
 updates too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave 2 of the Zeo next proposal (docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §5), review
debt found in the 0.5.1 bump review: patches 0029 and 0034 read the
Claude adapter's `_meta` — `_claude/backgroundTasks.count` for the
sidebar's Background status, `_claude/tasks` for the task list — inside
the `acp_v1::SessionUpdate::SessionInfoUpdate` arm only. A v2 agent's
session info update goes through `InboundSessionUpdate::SessionInfo`
(agent_servers/src/acp/session_updates.rs), which called
`update_session_info` and nothing else, so for a v2 agent both stayed
empty. PARITY-REPORT §24.1 measured the same gap from the other side.

The reading moves, unchanged, into `AcpThread::apply_claude_task_meta`,
and both arms call it before `update_session_info`. Its rules are the
ones 0029 and 0034 wrote: a missing key is "no change", never "no tasks",
and a malformed snapshot is logged by category and position only.

Claude Agent (Plus) speaks v1, so nothing changes for it; this matters
the day an agent sends the same `_meta` over v2. The v2 `_meta` is a
patch (`MaybeUndefined`); a `null` or absent one carries no keys, which
is again "no change".

Test: agent_servers acp::v1 tests,
`v2_session_info_carries_the_claude_task_meta`, through the real v2
harness. Verified 2026-11-09 in the prepared d2a4fb6 tree: cargo check --tests, cargo clippy --tests and cargo fmt --check clean, cargo test passing, on acp_thread, agent_servers, agent_ui and sidebar.
---

